# Line endings are settled here rather than by hand.
#
# The repository stores LF for every text file. What sits in the working tree is
# not our business: this folder is edited from Windows and synced through a
# mount that rewrites files with CRLF whenever it feels like it, and chasing
# that was costing more than it was worth. `text=auto eol=lf` makes git
# normalise on the way in and on comparison, so a file whose line endings
# flipped no longer reads as a file that was rewritten.
#
# It is only ever a diff problem. Lua does not care, WoW does not care and the
# packager does not care -- but a file that flips shows up as every line
# changed, which buries the one line that really changed and takes `git blame`
# with it. That happened once, at 12,829 lines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched. Listed explicitly because `text=auto` guesses from
# content, and a .tga that happens to contain no null bytes early on can be
# guessed wrong -- at which case git would "fix" the line endings inside an
# image.
*.tga binary
*.blp binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.png binary
